bl:Evidence_StoryDeepRAGSubjectCleanup a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Regression suite rewritten, live content cleaned, SPARQL playground and Code Lab demo fixed and verified"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.15.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "661e4eb88ea2103bc97100b49b52e1c831b5e621371c7cbfe12c3d48249bcca0" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium); real Pyodide execution" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryDeepRAGSubjectCleanup ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Real, functionally-critical progress, not yet complete: established a precise, real baseline first by running the actual REGRESSION_QUESTIONS suite (fusedCorpusAnswer, no live LLM needed) via Playwright against this corpus's own real data before touching anything -- 11/24 already passed (subject-agnostic structural tests), 13/24 genuinely failed because they referenced the source subject's own P01-P20 IDs and 'LC Waikiki principles' phrasing. Investigated retrieveContext directly first: confirmed its own 'LCW principles' reference is dead code, gated behind a company-name match that can never fire since COMPANY_DATA.companies is empty for this corpus -- the retrieval logic itself was already correct, only the test suite's hardcoded expectations were stale. Rewrote all 13 failing entries with real questions about this corpus's own content, preserving each original's structural lesson (explicit-identifier priority, enumeration, multi-entry naming, honest hedging under embedding-free semantic uncertainty) -- every single replacement verified individually via real Playwright execution against the real fusedCorpusAnswer before being written into the suite, not assumed to behave equivalently. Re-ran the complete suite after assembly: 24/24 passing, 0 console/page errors. UPDATE (this pass): fixed the real SPARQL-playground placeholders (a live button, two input placeholders, and a live 'help' response, all referencing a nonexistent id), verified the corrected SPARQL example via real Oxigraph execution; fixed a genuinely broken, real executable Code Lab demo ('Reinforcement chains') that referenced nonexistent principle ids and would have crashed with a KeyError if run -- replaced with two real ids (AgentPlatformPillar, genuinely reinforcement-free; SynthesisAndImplications, a genuine 6-hop chain) and verified by actually running the corrected snippet through runCode() and real Pyodide, not just reading the text. Found and fixed a second large subject-specific embedded constant (PROV_TTL, an entire real turn-by-turn build history of the OTHER project) feeding the same live Oxigraph engine as BIAS_TTL/AGENTIC_TTL -- emptied using the same proven pattern, verified via a real reload (120 triples, 0 errors, the real corpus's own SPARQL query still returns correct rows). Remaining, still disclosed: genuine historical developer comments (accurate, not user-facing, left alone per this session's own established reasoning)." .

