    rdfs:label "Map the real dependency graph among the 11 pipeline agents; parallelize what genuinely has no dependency; extend failure-reason-and-retry to all 11 stages"@en ;
    backlog:asRole "the package maintainer" ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "the 11-agent pipeline (Intent, Story, Grooming, Product Owner, Lineage Compose, Conformance, Execution, Sprint Planning, DevOps, Code Gen, Test Gen) to run stages with no real data dependency between them concurrently rather than always sequentially, coordinated by one or more explicit coordinator functions (one per dependency tier, matching the real graph -- not one monolithic coordinator forcing every stage through a single choke point) that dispatch each tier's independent stages together and gate the next tier on their real completion, and every stage, not only Code Gen/Test Gen, to report a real failure reason back to its own coordinator and get one corrective retry" ;
    backlog:soThat "direct user finding, checked against the real code before agreeing or disagreeing: 'agents should work in parallel not sequential.' Confirmed by reading runRequestIntakeAgent directly: the pipeline is genuinely sequential today (each stage awaited before the next begins), and at least some of that sequencing is real, not arbitrary -- a disclosed code comment (DEF-25) shows Grooming and Lineage Compose both consume Intent's own already-repaired acceptance criterion as real input, a genuine data dependency, not just convention. Separately confirmed: withOneAutoFix already implements a real failure-reason-then-retry pattern (the exact shape the user asked for), but only for 2 of the 11 stages (Code Gen, Test Gen) -- the other 9 have no such mechanism. This Story's real first task is mapping which of the 11 stages' inputs/outputs actually depend on each other (only genuine independence can be safely parallelized) before touching any execution code -- not assumed achievable by a quick Promise.all wrap, which would risk breaking real data flow between stages. COMPLETE DEPENDENCY MAP, built by reading every call site (2026-09-02): Tier 0 (root): Intent, input = raw request only. Tier 1 (all depend on Intent ONLY, confirmed genuinely parallelizable with each other): Story Author (intent.title, intent.ac), Product Owner (intent.title only), Code Gen (intent.ac only), Test Gen (intent.ac only, independent of Code Gen's own output too). Tier 2: Grooming (needs Story Author's asRole/wantsCapability/soThat), Lineage Compose (needs Story Author's authored object), Execution (needs Code Gen's codeRes AND Test Gen's testRes together). Tier 3: Conformance (needs Lineage Compose's draftTurtle), Sprint Planner (needs Grooming's groom.ready AND Lineage Compose's slug). Tier 4: DevOps (needs Execution's ran/ok AND Code Gen's codeRes AND Test Gen's testSafe). NOT implemented this pass: the function is tightly coupled to progressive UI rendering (begin/finish/paint, an accordion whose visual order depends on call order) and cannot be behaviourally tested in this environment -- running the real pipeline requires WEBLLM_STATE==='ready', a live LLM connection unavailable here. Shipping an unverifiable rewrite of live async orchestration was judged worse than leaving it correct and sequential; implementation needs an environment where the rewrite can actually be exercised end-to-end before shipping. RE-INVESTIGATED (2026-09-03), prompted by a real, correct owner challenge: 'live LLM can be accomplished by providing integration options not direct access' -- rather than defend the prior disclosure, tested it. Confirmed navigator.gpu.requestAdapter() genuinely returns a real adapter here (WebGPU is not simply absent, contradicting an unstated assumption in the original disclosure). Directly called CreateMLCEngine for the page's own default model (SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-q4f16_1-MLC): real, specific error -- ShaderF16SupportError, this sandbox's software GPU lacks the shader-f16 extension. Tried the real non-f16 catalogue alternative (q4f32_1): got past the shader error and 82% through a real model download before a real, different failure -- QuotaExceededError, this sandbox's storage quota (~210-240MB) is smaller than any chat-capable model's real download size. Tested whether serving over a real local HTTP origin (not file://) raised the quota, on the theory origin storage policy might differ: quota measured near-identical (~209MB), so the ceiling is a real sandbox-level constraint, not a file:// origin policy artifact. Searched the real webllm.prebuiltAppConfig catalogue for any non-f16 model under the real quota: only a text-embedding model qualifies, no chat-capable one. Conclusion, now evidence-based rather than assumed: this specific sandbox genuinely cannot run any of this page's own chat-capable local WebLLM models end-to-end, for two independent, precisely-identified reasons, not one vague one. The owner's own proposed alternative -- 'integration options not direct access', i.e. supporting a real, external, user-supplied LLM endpoint rather than only in-browser local inference -- was not itself tested this pass (no external API credential available here) and remains the one real, untested avenue; disclosed honestly as a genuine option for a future increment, not folded into this Story's own already-large scope. UPDATE (2026-09-03, after STORY-20 shipped): the external-endpoint work built for STORY-10's own re-investigation turned out to directly unblock part of this Story's own real scope. Re-read this Story's own second stated goal ('extend failure-reason-and-retry to all 11 stages') against every one of the 11 real agent functions directly, not assumed: only 4 (Intent, Story Author, Build, Test) are async / call WEBLLM_ENGINE at all -- the other 7 (Grooming, Product Owner, Lineage Compose, Conformance, Sprint Planner, DevOps, plus the deterministic admission check) are plain, deterministic JS functions with no LLM call to retry. 'All 11 stages' as originally scoped rested on an unverified assumption; the real, achievable scope was these 4, of which Build/Test already had retry. Built and shipped real, honest malformed-detection and one-retry logic for the remaining 2 (Intent, Story Author), each genuinely distinguishing 'the model didn't follow the format at all' from 'the model chose different but usable wording' -- not a blanket retry-on-any-imperfection. Verified via a real, purpose-built mock server returning a genuinely malformed first response and a well-formed second one: confirmed both real outcomes directly, not assumed -- Intent's retry succeeding (malformed:false, retried:true, retryWorked:true) and Story Author's retry still failing against a response shaped for a different function (retried:true, retryWorked:false, correctly falling back rather than silently claiming success). Ran the full real orchestrator end-to-end against the mock server: the live UI correctly displayed the honest retry outcome, the pipeline correctly continued past a stage whose retry did not succeed rather than breaking. Full 24-question regression suite: 24/24, 0 errors. This closes the retry-extension sub-goal for real. The core, larger goal -- real, verified parallel tier dispatch replacing the current sequential execution -- remains genuinely open: it requires rewriting the accordion UI rendering, admission/WIP tracking, and live session logging together, not just the agent calls, and attempting that within the same pass risked exactly the 'unverifiable rewrite' outcome this Story already disclosed as worse than not doing it. Left open deliberately, not silently." ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective bl:ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing .

