bl:AC_StoryConformanceFixAndMenuCleanup a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "The pipeline's Conformance stage passes on a real run, and the Explorer sidebar shows no duplicate navigation"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the same pipeline request the user's own uploaded session log recorded ('Find the sentences where a word or text exist within the corpus'), When the Lineage Compose and Conformance stages run, Then Conformance no longer reports 'A team must name the register or project it delivers from' -- checked by reproducing the exact SHACL merge the browser worker performs, not assumed. And Given the Principle Explorer's sidebar, When a reader looks at it, Then no block duplicates the always-visible top navigation bar." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "LINEAGE_TTL (JS const in code_abundance_page_v1_12_0.html)" .

bl:Evidence_StoryConformanceFixAndMenuCleanup a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.34.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "fe52ea84d7af06451a7d9c1b4a5f6ec74f6bf378c4f4549c7f648d47540d092c" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Conformance bug root-caused and fixed via real pyshacl reproduction; duplicate menu block removed"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "User uploaded a real session log (lcwkb_session_log_2026-09-02T08-35-24-966Z.zip) recording an actual pipeline run whose Conformance stage failed with a precise, quoted SHACL message: 'http://example.org/lcw-principles-kb#CodeAbundance_Team: A team must name the register or project it delivers from.' Traced to its exact cause, not guessed: found the generated draft Turtle's ex:CodeAbundance_Team individual correctly asserts backlog:teamFor ex:Backlog, but ex:Backlog itself is never given a type anywhere in the merged validation graph -- because LINEAGE_TTL, one of the 5 graphs merged for validation, had been emptied to an empty string during this session's own earlier STORY-3 cleanup (correctly removing the prior subject's stale lineage history) without providing a minimal valid replacement for this subject. Reproduced the exact failure with real pyshacl outside the browser, matching the SHACL worker's own merge logic exactly (read directly from shaclWorkerSource(): TBOX+ABOX+LINEAGE+DRAFT merged into one data graph, SHAPES+RULES into the shapes graph) -- confirmed byte-for-byte reproduction of the reported message. Fixed by adding a minimal, real declaration (ex:Backlog a backlog:Backlog) to LINEAGE_TTL; re-ran the identical pyshacl reproduction against the live, patched file and confirmed the violation is gone. Separately, user reported: 'Principle explorer's second left menu is not adding value, it repeats the left most menu' -- confirmed real: an 'All Sections' jump-tree inside the Explorer sidebar duplicated the same 6 destinations already reachable from the always-visible top nav bar. Removed it; confirmed its click-handler was already null-guarded (if(jumpRow){...}), so removal introduces no error. Re-verified via real Playwright after both fixes: 0 console/page errors, confirmed via fresh screenshot that the sidebar no longer shows the duplicate block." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium); pyshacl" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryConformanceFixAndMenuCleanup .

