bl:AC_StoryMsExplorerRedesign a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "The sidebar shows short labels only, with icons, and clicking a category filters the middle list to its own contents"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the Principle Explorer's left tree and middle list, When a reader looks at any row, Then it shows only a short label with an icon (folder for categories, document for principles), never the raw ontology identifier. And Given a reader clicks a category in the left tree, When the middle panel updates, Then it shows only that category's own items with a count and a 'Show all' control to reset -- real folder-click behaviour, not a second, always-everything duplicate of the tree." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "renderExplorerList (JS function in code_abundance_page_v1_12_0.html)" .

bl:Evidence_StoryMsExplorerRedesign a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.34.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "fe52ea84d7af06451a7d9c1b4a5f6ec74f6bf378c4f4549c7f648d47540d092c" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Sidebar redesigned to MS-Explorer style: raw IDs removed, icons added, real folder-click filtering wired up and verified"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "User attached the actual rendered text content of the sidebar, showing the real problem precisely: every row showed the raw ontology identifier (e.g. 'AgentPlatformPillar') stacked directly above/beside its readable label, and the middle panel repeated all 18 items flatly regardless of tree selection -- a genuine second view of the same data, not previously distinguished from the 'All Sections' duplicate already removed. Traced both to their exact source: the tree-row template concatenated a mono-styled ${p.id} span with the label span; the middle #explorer-list panel rendered all PRINCIPLES unconditionally with no connection to the tree's own selection state. Fixed by: (1) removing the visible raw-id span from both the tree-row and the mini-card, keeping it only in aria-label/title for accessibility; (2) adding lightweight Unicode icons (folder for categories, document for principles) for a real MS-Explorer visual grammar; (3) extracting the middle list's rendering into a real, callable renderExplorerList() function gated by a new EXPLORER_LIST_FILTER state variable, and wiring the existing category-toggle click handler to set that filter and re-render -- genuine folder-click behaviour (click a category, see only its contents, with a count and a 'Show all N' reset), not a cosmetic change. One real authoring bug caught and fixed during this same build, before shipping: an initial version of renderExplorerList() had backslash-escaped backticks/dollar-braces inside a plain JS string, producing invalid syntax -- caught by directly re-reading the written file content, not assumed correct from the edit script's own success, and rewritten with plain string concatenation. FOLLOW-UP PASS, same session: a broader, real Playwright check (searching for the raw string 'AgentPlatformPillar' anywhere in the rendered DOM, not only in the two panels the user's screenshot showed) found the same defect class in 8 further places this Story's original scope had not covered: the detail-pane .pnum heading (two separate rendering functions, principleCardHTML and principleDetailHTML), the 'reinforces' chip generator, a 'Quick jump' widget on the Overview tab, two natural-language chat-answer templates, and the 'Copy as AI prompt' feature's own prompt text -- the last of which was also found to still say 'LC Waikiki' verbatim, a genuine miss from the earlier STORY-7 cleanup pass. All 8 fixed the same way: raw id removed from visible/generated text, real label used instead. One further instance (inside buildCompanyView, gated on the now-empty COMPANY_DATA.themes array) confirmed dead code that never executes for this subject, left as-is rather than edited pointlessly. Re-verified comprehensively via real Playwright across Explorer, Overview, Citations and About tabs, plus the actual filter-click/reset/detail-select interaction: 0 remaining raw-id matches anywhere in the rendered DOM except one legitimate SVG <title> tooltip element (the relation-map graph's own accessibility hover-text, appropriately more detailed, not a menu). 0 console/page errors throughout. Re-ran all Stage1-3 gates fresh: all PASS." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium)" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryMsExplorerRedesign .

