bl:AC_StoryPackageInstallAnalysis a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "The Conformance fix is confirmed working in a real user session, and network/package-import refusals get a stronger, targeted retry"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the user's own uploaded session log recording a real pipeline run, When the Conformance stage's real result is read, Then it shows 'done, 0 Violation-severity results', confirming the earlier LINEAGE_TTL fix genuinely holds outside this session's own testing. And Given Code Gen or Test Gen refuses code for a network or package-related reason, When the automatic retry runs, Then the correction message restates the exact constraint (no network, no pip, use only the local data and standard library) rather than a generic 'fix it' note." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "await micropip.install (JS call in code_abundance_page_v1_12_0.html's SHACL worker, the real evidence the analysis was grounded in)" .

bl:Evidence_StoryPackageInstallAnalysis a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.34.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "fe52ea84d7af06451a7d9c1b4a5f6ec74f6bf378c4f4549c7f648d47540d092c" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Real analysis of the package-installation question, grounded in the actual code and a real user session log; retry message strengthened"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "User uploaded a real session log showing a genuine pipeline run's Conformance stage now reporting 'done, 0 Violation-severity results' -- direct, independent confirmation the earlier LINEAGE_TTL fix (STORY-11) genuinely holds in real use, not only in this session's own reproduction. The same log's real Code Gen failure ('a network/HTTP import; a package not available here (requests, bs4)... no pip installs') was investigated by reading the actual code, not assumed: found the code-gen system prompt already explicitly forbids network imports and pip installs and explicitly instructs the model to use the real local data (principles/categories/frameworks/relations/company data, already loaded as Python variables) -- the model ignored this instruction on its first attempt regardless, and the automatic one-shot retry used only a generic 'fix it: <reason>' correction rather than restating the specific constraint, so the retry failed the same way. Separately confirmed, by reading the actual SHACL worker's own working code, that package installation via micropip IS technically functional in this browser environment for at least one real case (pyshacl) -- the refusal here is a deliberate safety design choice (a hardcoded regex blocking requests/urllib/http.client/socket imports specifically), not a platform-level impossibility, and the main Pyodide instance used by Code Gen/Execution never calls micropip.install for anything, unlike the separate SHACL worker instance. Fixed the one safe, bounded improvement available without changing the underlying model or safety policy: network/package-flagged retries now receive a specific, forceful restatement of the real constraint (no network, no pip, local data and stdlib only) instead of a generic note. Re-verified via real Playwright, including a direct logic test of the new branch: 0 console/page errors, correct behaviour confirmed." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium); pyshacl" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryPackageInstallAnalysis .

