    rdfs:label "Confirm the Conformance fix in real use, and analyze the package-installation question with a real, targeted improvement"@en ;
    backlog:asRole "a reader running the pipeline, and the package maintainer"@en ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "confirmation that the earlier Conformance fix genuinely works outside this session, and a grounded, evidence-based answer to whether package installation is possible at all here, whether a different language would help, and what a safe next step looks like" ;
    backlog:soThat "user's uploaded session log confirmed the Conformance fix in real use, and asked directly: is package installation possible at all, should a different language be used instead of Python, or are there other ways to install or reuse packages. Answered by reading the real code rather than guessing: package installation IS technically functional here (proven by the SHACL worker's own working micropip call), the refusal is a deliberate safety choice not a platform limit, and the specific observed failure was an LLM instruction-compliance issue -- the system prompt already correctly forbade network access -- not a missing capability." ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective bl:ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing .

bl:Estimate_Story14 a backlog:CostEstimate, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Cost estimate: STORY-14 (real package installation, generic failure-communication)"@en ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate "4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasCostBasis "Judged: two real, substantial pieces -- wiring micropip into the main Pyodide instance across both execution paths (pipeline and standalone Code Lab), and redesigning failure objects to carry their own remedy so retries stop guessing from label text -- each independently verified, including a genuine end-to-end install-and-run test, not just a logic check." ;
    backlog:hasEstimateConfidence "High"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

bl:AC_StoryRealPackageInstall a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "A curated set of real packages actually installs and runs, and failure objects carry their own remedy consumed generically"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given Python code importing numpy, pandas, or networkx, When it runs in either the pipeline's Execution stage or the standalone Code Lab, Then the package is actually installed via a real micropip call before the code runs, and the code's own real output is produced -- not a ModuleNotFoundError. And Given any safety check in extractAndCheckCode flags a violation, When withOneAutoFix builds its retry, Then it uses that check's own remedy field directly, with no code in withOneAutoFix inspecting the violation's label text or guessing its category." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "ensureSafePackagesInstalled (JS function in code_abundance_page_v1_12_0.html)" .

