    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "PACKAGE INSTALLATION: loaded micropip into the main Pyodide instance (ensurePyodide()), matching the pattern already proven working by the separate SHACL-checking worker. Curated a small, real, named allowlist (numpy, pandas, networkx -- genuinely useful for analysing this project's own local data, no network/scraping libraries) shared as a single global set between the safety-check logic, the pipeline's Execution stage, and the standalone Code Lab's runCode(), rather than three places that could drift. Wired a new ensureSafePackagesInstalled() helper into both real execution paths. Verified with the strongest test available, not a logic-only check: actually loaded real Pyodide in a real headless browser, called micropip.install(['numpy']) for real, and ran real numpy code (np.array([1,2,3]).sum() == 6, confirmed) -- then repeated for pandas (DataFrame sum == 6, confirmed) and networkx (graph edge count == 1, confirmed). Non-curated packages (e.g. requests, bs4) remain refused, with a remedy naming the real allowed set. GENERIC FAILURE-COMMUNICATION: removed the prior turn's own case-by-case regex guess (/network|http|package|pip|import/i) from withOneAutoFix, which the user correctly identified as exactly the case-by-case pattern being asked to avoid generically. Redesigned instead: every entry in suspiciousPatterns, and the non-stdlib-package check, now carries its own remedy field -- the exact, actionable correction stated once, at the point that actually knows what happened. withOneAutoFix was rewritten to generically join and use whatever remedies are present on first.flagged, with no inspection of label text and no per-case branching -- a new check added later works correctly here with zero change to this function, which is what makes it generic rather than case-by-case. Re-verified via real Playwright: 0 console/page errors; direct logic test confirmed the generic remedy path produces the expected corrected task text." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium)" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryRealPackageInstall .

