    rdfs:label "Enable real package installation for a curated safe set, and make failure-to-retry communication genuinely generic"@en ;
    backlog:asRole "the package maintainer" ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "genuine package installation for legitimate, safe analysis packages, and a failure-communication mechanism where each check states its own remedy once, generically consumed, rather than the receiving agent guessing per case" ;
    backlog:soThat "user asked directly: enable the package installation, and make agent-return information generic enough for receiving agents to act on without case-by-case correction like the specific fix made last turn. Both delivered: real, end-to-end-verified micropip installation for a curated safe set (network/scraping libraries still refused, on purpose, as a different and still-necessary safety boundary), and a remedy field on every check that withOneAutoFix consumes generically -- removing the exact case-by-case regex this Story's own request was pointing at." ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective bl:ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing .

bl:Estimate_Story15 a backlog:CostEstimate, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Cost estimate: STORY-15 (near-miss package hints, token-budget-aware retry)"@en ;
    backlog:hasEffortEstimate "3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasCostBasis "Judged: user's uploaded session log gave two exact, real failures -- a package-name typo, and a genuine output-truncation the automatic retry made no better. Both root-caused from the real code; the token-budget fix required a small but real architectural change (threading a generation-config override through both code-gen functions), not just new text." ;
    backlog:hasEstimateConfidence "Medium"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:estimatedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasBasisKind backlog:Basis_Judged .

bl:AC_StoryGenericRetryStrategy a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "A near-miss package name gets a 'did you mean' hint, and a truncated retry gets a genuinely larger output budget, both generically"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given code importing a package within edit-distance 2 of a real installable package, When the safety check flags it, Then the remedy names the likely intended package by real edit-distance comparison against the actual allowed set, not a hardcoded pairing. And Given a generation reply with finish_reason=length, When withOneAutoFix builds its retry, Then the retry call uses a genuinely larger max_tokens, read generically from the flagged entry's own retryGenConfig, with no code in withOneAutoFix specific to truncation." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "withOneAutoFix (JS function in code_abundance_page_v1_12_0.html)" .

bl:Evidence_StoryGenericRetryStrategy a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.34.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "fe52ea84d7af06451a7d9c1b4a5f6ec74f6bf378c4f4549c7f648d47540d092c" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Both real failures from the uploaded log root-caused and fixed generically; end-to-end verified including exact reproduction of the logged typo"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-02T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "User uploaded a real session log with two distinct real failures. (1) Build stage: 'a package not available here (networks)' -- the model wrote networks (not a real package) instead of networkx (genuinely installable, per STORY-14). Confirmed the existing remedy already named networkx correctly as part of the allowed set, and the model still repeated the same mistake on its one automatic retry -- a real LLM reliability limit text alone did not overcome. Added a generic near-miss hint: real Levenshtein edit-distance between each refused import and every name in the actual PYODIDE_SAFE_PACKAGES set (not a hardcoded networks-means-networkx pairing), surfaced in the remedy when distance <= 2. Verified by reproducing the exact logged code (import networks) through the real extractAndCheckCode function: remedy text now reads exactly \"'networks' is not a real package -- did you mean 'networkx'?\", generically derived. (2) Test stage: 'the model hit its output budget...finish_reason=length', still unsafe after 1 automatic retry. Root cause found by reading the real retry code: the prior remedy for this case had no dedicated remedy at all, so the retry used the old generic 'fix it: <reason>' text -- which, for a token-budget failure specifically, makes the retry's own prompt LONGER, needing MORE output room, not less, working against itself. Fixed generically: truncationFlag() now carries a deliberately short remedy (asking for conciseness, not added explanation) plus a structured retryGenConfig (a genuinely larger max_tokens); agentCodeGen and agentTestGen both accept an optional genConfigOverride threaded into their real WEBLLM_ENGINE call; withOneAutoFix generically merges every flagged entry's own retryGenConfig (Object.assign across all present) and passes it to the retry call, with no special-case code for truncation specifically -- a future check needing a different generation-config change works here unmodified. Verified via real Playwright direct logic tests (Levenshtein distance, truncationFlag's remedy/retryGenConfig shape, the generic merge producing the correct boosted max_tokens) and a full real reproduction of the exact logged typo through the actual extractAndCheckCode pipeline, confirmed byte-for-byte. 0 console/page errors. Re-ran all Stage1-3 gates fresh: all PASS." ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium)" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryGenericRetryStrategy .

bl:StoryGenericRetryStrategy a backlog:Story, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "STORY-15" ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasActualEffort "4"^^xsd:decimal ;
