    backlog:startedAt "2026-09-02T14:53:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:finishedAt "2026-09-02T14:53:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-09-02T14:53:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasEvidence bl:Evidence_StoryGenericRetryStrategy ;
    backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion bl:AC_StoryGenericRetryStrategy ;
    backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Automated ;
    backlog:memberOfContainer bl:CodeAbundanceBacklog ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone bl:DoDCodeAbundance ;
    backlog:hasCostEstimate bl:Estimate_Story15 ;
    backlog:dependsOn bl:StoryRealPackageInstall ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_TechnicalDebt ;
    rdfs:label "Handle a not-available package and a token-budget failure with generic, structured retry information, not case-specific text"@en ;
    backlog:asRole "the package maintainer"@en ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "a package-name typo to get a real, evidence-based correction hint, and a token-budget failure to get a genuinely bigger retry budget rather than a longer prompt that makes the same problem worse -- both delivered through the same generic remedy/retryGenConfig mechanism, no new case-specific branches in the retry logic itself" ;
    backlog:soThat "user's uploaded session log showed both failures for real: a package typo the existing remedy already named correctly but the model still missed, and a truncated test-gen reply whose one automatic retry failed the same way because appending more explanation only asked for more room, not less. Both root-caused from the real code and fixed through the same generic mechanism STORY-14 established -- remedy and retryGenConfig read directly off each flagged entry, with zero per-case logic added to withOneAutoFix itself." ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective bl:ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing .

