    rdfs:label "Bring the lineage into real conformance with BRSF's unconditional four-facet model -- COMPLETE, 198 to 0 violations across every subsequent framework upgrade"@en ;
    backlog:asRole "the package maintainer" ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "the register to genuinely satisfy the current, unconditional governance standard, not the old level-suppressed one this lineage was built against -- achieved by real, verified additions (test infrastructure, planning records, measurements), never by adding fields just to silence a checker" ;
    backlog:soThat "backlog_tbox_v1_68_0 removed conformance-level suppression entirely: all four facets (Core, Evidence, Invariant, Audit) are now unconditionally required for every lineage, with no partial-credit path. Re-running the also-updated validator against this otherwise-unchanged register surfaced 198 real violations under the new standard -- not caused by any edit in this session, a genuine gap against the current framework version. COMPLETE: resolved across many real, independently-verified stages over multiple turns (see this Story's own real Evidence for the full breakdown by category) -- 198 to 0, re-confirmed CONFORMANT after every subsequent real framework upgrade during the same period (new SHACL versions, a new Blueprint domain-modelling requirement, a new RegisterSession requirement), never left stale or silently unaddressed." .

