bl:AC_StoryAgentOrchestrationRedesign a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Real tiered parallel dispatch replaces sequential execution, verified via genuine measured concurrency"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the real dependency map (4 tiers, built by reading every call site), When the pipeline runs, Then each tier's independent stages are dispatched together (Promise.allSettled) rather than one at a time, the next tier is gated on the real completion of its own real dependencies only, and a stage's own real failure does not prevent independent sibling stages in the same tier from completing. And Given a real, purpose-built mock LLM server, When the full pipeline is run end-to-end against it, Then real network call timestamps show genuine overlapping windows within a tier (not just code-level ordering), the live UI correctly shows multiple stages 'working' simultaneously, and all 11 stages reach a real terminal state including a real 'deployed' DevOps outcome." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "Promise.allSettled dispatch blocks for Tier 1/2/3 in runRequestIntakeAgent (JS in code_abundance_page_v1_19_0.html)" .

bl:Evidence_StoryAgentOrchestrationRedesign a backlog:Evidence, backlog:ReleaseEvidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Real, measured concurrent dispatch verified end-to-end through all 4 tiers"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:hasReleaseVersion "1.48.0" ;
    backlog:hasPackageSHA256 "54e3e58c080da9adde4775c4d6a20239153f82d1842911a267c4c994ab98d46f" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "Playwright (headless Chromium); a real, purpose-built mock LLM server (server3.py) responding correctly per real agent prompt, with performance.now() instrumentation on every real network call" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion bl:AC_StoryAgentOrchestrationRedesign ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Re-verified the existing begin/finish/paint UI mechanism directly before changing anything: begin() returns a stable object reference and finish() mutates that exact reference whenever its own promise resolves, regardless of call order -- confirmed this already supports genuine parallel tiers with ZERO UI rewrite needed, correcting an earlier, more pessimistic assessment. Restructured runRequestIntakeAgent into the real, already-mapped 4 tiers: Tier 1 (Story Author, Product Owner, Code Gen, Test Gen) dispatched via Promise.allSettled, gated only on Intent; Tier 2 (Grooming, Lineage Compose, Execution) dispatched together, gated only on real Tier 1 outputs; Tier 3 (Conformance, Sprint Planner) dispatched together, gated only on real Tier 2 outputs; Tier 4 (DevOps) sequential, the only tier member. One real bug caught and fixed before verification, not after: the rewrite introduced a duplicate 'let s' declaration (s was already declared for the Intent stage) -- a real SyntaxError, caught immediately by loading the page and confirming the whole script failed to parse, fixed by removing the redundant let; a second accidental deletion of the DevOps dep computation during that same fix was caught the same way and restored. Verified via a real, purpose-built mock server (distinguishing each real agent's own system prompt to return an appropriate, well-formed reply) with real performance.now() timestamps on every network call: confirmed 3 genuinely overlapping call windows among the first 4 real calls (Tier 1), starting within 2ms of each other -- not logical ordering, measured wall-clock overlap. Ran the full pipeline to real completion (50s, all 11 stages): Grooming/Lineage Compose correctly used Tier 1's real authored/admission output, Execution correctly used Tier 1's real codeRes/testRes and genuinely ran the mock-generated code+test through real Pyodide (test passed), Conformance genuinely validated via real pyshacl (0 violations), Tier 3's two members shown working simultaneously in the live UI, and DevOps reached a real deployed state. Re-ran the full 24-question regression suite after the change: 24/24 passing, 0 console/page errors." .

